 "note": "Authentic Raze 2 arms baked from DefineSprite_387 (arm1) and DefineSprite_136 (arm2). Split on the two axes the SWF itself splits on: the arm/hand parts are SKIN strips, the gun is the DefineSprite_380 strip indexed by curGun.sprite. So a skin sheet (skin/<skin>/<pose>.png) carries the arm art for every weapon sharing that pose, and a gun sheet (gun/<weapon>.png) carries just the weapon. A skin sheet holds three bands of `count` cells -- back (armup+armlow+hand1), front (hand2), arm2 -- because the gun draws between hand1 and hand2; cell index is band*count+frame. All four layers share one cell and one `anchor` (the shoulder), since UnitMC.as:103-109 gives arm1 and arm2 the same origin.",
